## Context

After tracker 1382 closed (PR #2098), the author asked whether monitoring is
now frictionless. The 2026-10-31 raid session (5e95a6, tickets 1390–1397)
hit these rough edges; the author said "Do it" to one small PR. Below the
ticket floor individually, bundled here. Gaze seat labelling stays ticket 1388.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `trace_timeline.py <prefix>` resolves a unique session-id prefix
      (live tree and archive); an ambiguous prefix lists the candidates and
      exits non-zero; the change stays inside session lookup (ticket 1397
      edits the HTML part of the same file in parallel)
- [ ] `raid_log.py append` refuses an event missing the keys its row in
      `skills/raid/references/sitrep.md` requires (`WAVE n= tickets=`,
      `PR n= ticket= step=` with step in the documented set, `QUEUE n=`
      numeric, …), naming the missing key and the expected form; one source
      of truth for the key table (no second copy drifting from the doc)
- [ ] `merge-gate.py run --model <bare id>` either accepts a known bare id by
      qualifying it (claude-* → anthropic/, gpt-* → openai/) or its error
      names the expected `provider/model-id` form with an example; no silent
      skip of the gate record
- [ ] (judgment) the bookkeeping-tier landing of a PR with no review prints an
      informational "no review (bookkeeping)" line instead of
      "attribution: not derivable: review (none on notes)", if that is a
      one-site change; otherwise leave it and say why
- [ ] Tests for each change; `make check-fast` green
